-- title:
--   T-saturation of (T,X₀,X₁)-powers in a Drinfeld chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a domain which is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal, with a generator $\pi$ of that maximal ideal, so $\mathfrak m_W = (\pi)$. Let $T \in \mathfrak m_W$ be non-zero, and set $c = T^{q+1}$. Let $f, u, v$ be formal power series in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$, with $u$ and $v$ units, and suppose that $f$ agrees with the Drinfeld form $X_0 X_1^{q} - X_0^{q} X_1$ modulo $(X_0, X_1)^{q+2}$. Write $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(c)\,v - f\,u)$, where $C$ denotes the constant-coefficient embedding of $W$, and let $\mathfrak N \subseteq S$ be the ideal generated by the images of $C(T)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The assertion is that for every natural number $n$ and every $s \in S$, if $s$ times the image of $C(T)$ lies in $\mathfrak N^{n+1}$, then $s$ lies in $\mathfrak N^{n}$; equivalently $(\mathfrak N^{n+1} : T) = \mathfrak N^{n}$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the statement that the chart parameter $T$ is a superficial element of the ideal $\mathfrak N = (T, X_0, X_1)$ in the local chart ring of a Drinfeld-type equation $cv = fu$, a colon-ideal computation which amounts to $\bar T$ being a non-zero-divisor on the associated graded ring of $S$ along $\mathfrak N$. It is used in the analysis of the auxiliary full-level modular curve charts, where membership in weighted centre powers has to be deduced from membership after multiplication by a power of the parameter.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_mem_span_pow_of_mul_mem_span_pow_succ_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow.lean

